{"id": "TASK-20261018-ENFORCEMENT-SERIES", "status": "done", "date": "2026-10-18", "title": "Retrieve the code-enforcement case series at APN 167-472-08 and test whether a permanent certificate of occupancy exists", "laws": ["Law 15 (official records)"], "result": "13 cases retrieved (2012-2026). Decisive: CC2023-02189 records that CO2020-005184 was a TEMPORARY certificate of occupancy and that a permanent CofO was still required; no permanent CofO appears in Accela for the address. 2026 cases allege no conditioned/ventilation air in dormitory and restroom/shower spaces (2022 CBC 1202.1/1202.5, CMC 402.1). Also obtained fire permits F2020-005031/005032 (11,526 sq ft Sprung structure; sprinklers) and F2020-006947.", "evidence": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\ACCELA_CAPTURE_20261018", "manifest_sha256": "fec67c72f7af416293854b638e7b7066f7a8c63c157ce6cabdf11e5fc7227e18", "files": 35, "addendum": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\investigation_dossiers\\CAMERON_LANE_LEGISTAR_ACCELA_ADDENDUM_20261018.md", "addendum_sha256": "14ec637a9a64f042167abfad135bab616109330fa4a5c2a5524d8e0af904e94a"}
{"id": "TASK-20261018-GIS-NEIGHBORS", "status": "done", "date": "2026-10-18", "title": "Resolve surrounding parcels, true adjacency, block ownership and zoning for 167-472-08 / 167-472-09", "laws": ["Law 15 (official records)"], "result": "Subject block mapped: 167-472-08 (Lot 6, 0.7933987 ac) and 167-472-09 (Lot 7, 0.7933686 ac) form a 1.5868 ac assembly, both owned by HUNTINGTON BEACH HOUSING AUTHORITY, both zoned SP14 / GP M-sp. Shared-boundary test: -08 touches 167-472-07 (Houser Company) and -09; -09 touches -08 and 167-472-10 (YN Real Estate LLC). Citywide owner query returns EXACTLY two HBHA parcels. 28-parcel block table captured with owners, sale dates, doc numbers and use codes.", "evidence": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\CAMERON_LANE_GIS_RECORDER_20261018", "files": ["PARCEL_ASSEMBLY_AND_DEEDS.json", "ASSESSOR_BLOCK_167-472_28_PARCELS.json", "HBHA_OWNED_PARCELS_CITYWIDE.json", "PARCEL_ADJACENCY_CONFIRMED.json"]}
{"id": "TASK-20261018-RECORDER-CHAIN", "status": "done", "date": "2026-10-18", "title": "Pull the recorded chain of title for 17631 Cameron Ln / 17642 Beach Blvd from the OC Clerk-Recorder public index", "laws": ["Law 15 (official records)"], "result": "Recorder host moved to https://cr.occlerkrecorder.gov/RecorderWorksInternet/ (cr.ocgov.com times out). Grant deed 2020000420412 recorded 8/19/2020 (4 pp, Yamada trusts -> HBHA) AND memo option 2020000420413 same day (9 pp); grant deed 2021000002954 recorded 1/5/2021 (4 pp, Beach parcel). 18 instruments naming HBHA captured with numbers/dates/pages. Signed LOI 1/16/2020 recovered: Cameron $3,077,010 ($90/sf) + Beach option $3,089,250 expiring 7/31/2021 = $6,166,260. LIMITATION: deed images paywalled ('Images may not be viewed online'); consideration unverified; recorder parcel-index (SearchMode=7) returns empty for these APNs.", "evidence": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\CAMERON_LANE_GIS_RECORDER_20261018", "addendum": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\CAMERON_LANE_GIS_RECORDER_20261018\\CAMERON_LANE_PARCEL_ASSEMBLY_ADDENDUM_20261018.md", "addendum_sha256": "42bb8f5ef203d7341ab469f96a508f7a2fd4afaa975bee49c26ee9df51197838", "manifest_sha256": "336567c16c5765f57448d1d47f2c1fc659df728f5947cf008b252b8aaac45ca2", "files": 18}
{"id": "TASK-20261018-ADDRESS-RESOLUTION", "status": "done", "date": "2026-10-18", "title": "Test whether 17361 Cameron Ln and 17631 Cameron Ln exist as City-issued addresses; resolve the 17642 Beach Blvd contradiction", "laws": ["Law 15 (official records)"], "result": "Neither 17361 Cameron Ln nor 17631 Cameron Ln exists as an address point in the City master file (WebAddresses/MapServer/3); Cameron Ln runs 17532-17762. Both subject parcels were re-addressed to 17642 Beach Blvd under Appl 2020-0268 effective 12-14-2020 (Unit 100 on Lot 6, Unit 102 on Lot 7). '17631 CAMERON LN' survives only as the assessor situs field. The three-address contradiction is therefore an administrative record-integrity defect, not evidence of intent.", "evidence": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\CAMERON_LANE_GIS_RECORDER_20261018\\CAMERON_LANE_ADDRESS_MASTER.json"}
{"id": "TASK-20261018-LEGISTAR-WITHDRAWN-OCR", "status": "done", "date": "2026-10-18", "title": "OCR the withdrawn and tabled shelter items and extract the County agreement timeline", "laws": ["Law 15 (official records)"], "result": "20-1777 Hopkins memo (7/17/2020): item withdrawn from the 7/20 agenda and moved to CLOSED SESSION real property negotiation. 20-1761 Peterson item: separate Gothard St yard site, tabled after Ocean View School District objection (OVSD letter OCR'd). 20-1799 Luna-Reynosa PPT (8/3/2020) full text extracted: County agreement to stand up shelter on Cameron site dated 4/20/2020 (before any deed), County to pay for 75 beds, City pushed to 174 beds to hit the 60% threshold needed to enforce anti-camping rules, ~$4M County spend, EEC Phase I engaged 3/18/2020, OCHCA 5/22/2020 letter requiring asphalt cap.", "evidence": "C:\\Amd949609_Antigravity_v1\\evidence\\hbnc_records\\CAMERON_LANE_GIS_RECORDER_20261018\\OCR_TEXTS"}
